{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.StrangeletDoubleBeta","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.StrangeletDoubleBeta","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.descent_path","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.descent_path","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/strangelet-double-beta.lean#L67-L74","doc":"The descent path goes cinquefoil → figure-eight → trefoil:\n5 → 4 → 3 crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.strangelet_double_beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.strangelet_double_beta","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/strangelet-double-beta.lean#L56-L65","doc":"**Definitional unfolding** of the strangelet double-beta rate. The physical model — the\ninteraction descends through two Skein smoothings (cinquefoil → figure-eight → trefoil)\nwith rate proportional to `s⁴`, `s = skein_amplitude q = tanh(ln q)` the EM/strong ratio —\nis *encoded in the definition* `double_beta_rate q := (skein_amplitude q) ^ 4`; this lemma\nonly exposes that definition (the earlier `1 < q` hypothesis was unused and is dropped).\nThe descent derivation and the parameter-free `s⁴ ≈ 10⁻⁴` reading are narrative\n(`.md` / Ch. 7), NOT a Lean consequence of this equation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:strangelet-double-beta","label":"prop:strangelet-double-beta","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/strangelet-double-beta.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.figure_eight_crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.figure_eight_crossings","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/strangelet-double-beta.lean#L52-L54","doc":"The intermediate knot (figure-eight, 4₁) has 4 crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.trefoil_crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.trefoil_crossings","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/strangelet-double-beta.lean#L48-L50","doc":"The trefoil has 3 crossings (genus 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.cinquefoil_crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.cinquefoil_crossings","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/strangelet-double-beta.lean#L44-L46","doc":"The cinquefoil has 5 crossings (genus 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossing_descent_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossing_descent_count","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/strangelet-double-beta.lean#L37-L42","doc":"The Skein descent: the minimal path from the degree-2 fiber\n(cinquefoil, 5 crossings) to the degree-1 fiber (trefoil,\n3 crossings) requires exactly 2 crossing changes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.double_beta_rate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.double_beta_rate","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/strangelet-double-beta.lean#L32-L35","doc":"The double beta decay rate is proportional to s⁴. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skein_amplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skein_amplitude","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/strangelet-double-beta.lean#L26-L30","doc":"The Skein amplitude for a single crossing change:\ns(q) = q^{1/2} − q^{−1/2}. ","signatureChunk":0}]}